 "semantic_justification": {
  "position_setter_changes_are_entailed": true,
  "argument": "The _newlinesIn signature change (adding required endPosition) is the CR/LF fix for issue #80: it makes newline detection boundary-aware so that a trailing \\r is only counted when the next char is not \\n, eliminating the empty-list removeLast() RangeError. Because _newlinesIn now receives the full substring (from oldPosition) plus an endPosition, the returned match offsets (newlines.last.end) are relative to that substring; the position setter MUST combine them with oldPosition ('offsetOfLastNewline = oldPosition + newlines.last.end') to keep the existing column computation correct. The 'newPosition == position' early return and 'newPosition == 0' reset are defensive guards around the same reworked setter and are required for the reworked _newlinesIn call sites to behave identically to the previous scanner for all inputs. In other words, the position-setter column arithmetic is entailed by the CR/LF endPosition rework, not an independent defect: without the endPosition parameter the CR/LF boundary bug cannot be fixed, and once the parameter exists the setter arithmetic must follow. The upstream CHANGELOG lists them as separate bullets for release-note clarity, but they are one cohesive fix in the same function.",
  "evidence": "upstream commit 084b201c; fix commit message; issue #80 reproduction"
 },
